 "title": "Metro Auditor | Metro",
 "text": "Metro Auditor | Metro\nSkip to main content\ncollapse all\nEvents\nNews and stories\nTools and data\nContact\nLanguage hub\nWhat Metro does\nWhat Metro does\nProjects\nConnecting regional priorities\nGarbage and recycling system\nHousing and homelessness\nLand use and development\nParks and nature investments\nTransportation\nTools and data\nVisitor venues\nGet involved\nGet involved\nGive your input\nCommittees\nFind funding\nPublic engagement\nWaste disposal and prevention\nWaste disposal and prevention\nNeed to get rid of something?\nHealthy living and waste reduction\nReport dumped garbage\nEducation resources\nParks and nature\nParks and nature\nParks\nBoat ramps\nCemeteries\nGuided nature activities\nReservations and services\nSafety and policies\nAbout Metro\nAbout Metro\nMetro Council\nMetro Auditor\nMERC\nStructure and operations\nCivil rights at Metro\nMetro Code\nAccessibility at Metro\nEquity at Metro\nDoing business with Metro\nPublic records\nJobs\nEvents\nNews and stories\nTools and data\nContact\nLanguage hub\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\nAbout Metro\nMetro Council\nMetro Auditor\nMission and authority\nProcess and auditing standards\nAbout the Metro Auditor\nAudits\nAudit committee\nAccountability hotline\nSubmit ideas for future audit topics\nMERC\nStructure and operations\nCivil rights at Metro\nMetro Code\nAccessibility at Metro\nEquity at Metro\nDoing business with Metro\nPublic records\nJobs\nMetro Auditor\nThe Metro Auditor, elected region-wide, is responsible for conducting performance audits.\nRecently released audits\nFinancial Condition of Metro: FY 2015-16 to FY 2024-25\nThis June 2024 report provides a check-up to see how well Metro is doing financially, based on the indicators recommended by the International City/County Management Association.\nTransfer station operating controls follow-up audit\nThis May 2026 f ollow-up audit found progress was made on garbage and recycling transfer station operating controls recommendations.\nOregon Zoo bond implementation audit\nThis April 2026 audit found the Oregon Zoo was unprepared to implement the 2024 bond measure.\nAccountability hotline case 507 audit\nThis February 2026 audit found stronger controls are needed to prevent conflicts of interest.\nSupportive housing services follow-up audit\nThis November 2025 follow-up audit found progress had been made on Supportive Housing Services recommendations and identified opportunities for continued improvement.\nAccountability hotline case 495 audit\nThis October 2025 audit recommended prioritizing ethical requirements to set the reuse program up for success.\nMore audits\nAudit schedule\nAudit name | start date | expected completion date |\nAudit name Communications | start date February 2026 | expected completion date December 2026 |\nAudit name Accessibility | start date April 2026 | expected completion date December 2026 |\nAudit name Procurement cards | start date TBD | expected completion date TBD |\nAudit name Fleet management | start date TBD | expected completion date TBD |\nAudit name 2019 Parks and Nature bond follow-up | start date TBD | expected completion date TBD |\nAudit name Internal training and staff development | start date TBD | expected completion date TBD |\nAudit name Transparent Governance: FY 2016-17 to FY 2025-26 | start date October 2026 | expected completion date TBD |\nSubscribe to Metro audits\nThe Metro Auditor publishes announcements when each new audit is published. Sign up to be notified of new audit releases.\nSubscribe\nHave an audit idea?\nComplete this short online form to suggest a topic. Metro Auditor Brian Evans welcomes feedback from the public.\nShare your ideas\nRelated pages\nAbout the Metro Auditor\nMetro Auditor Brian Evans and staff are responsible for conducting performance audits and reviewing Metro operations with the purpose of improving efficiency, effectiveness, and equity.\nAccountability hotline\nThe Auditor’s Office administers the Metro Accountability Hotline. The hotline gives employees and the public an avenue to report fraud, waste or abuse of resources or position in any Metro or MERC facility or department.\nContact\nBrian Evans, Metro Auditor\nhe, him, his\nBrian.Evans@oregonmetro.gov 503-797-1891\nOpportunities\nGive your input\nJobs\nGrants and funding\nContracts\nServices\nAsk a garbage and recycling expert\nApply for a contractor's business license\nBuy a parks pass\nBuy a cemetery plot\nGet language assistance\nGet ADA assistance\nMetro employee hub\nPay my SHS tax\nLeadership\nMetro Council\nWho is my councilor?\nMetro Auditor\nCommittees\nWhether your roots in the region run generations deep or you moved to Oregon last week, you have your own reasons for loving this place — and Metro wants to keep it that way. Help shape the future of the greater Portland region and discover tools, services and places that make life better today.\nContact Metro\n503-797-1700\nRelay service 711\nSend a message\nOregon Convention Center\nOregon Zoo\nPortland Expo Center\nPortland'5 Centers for the Arts\nFind Metro on\n© Oregon Metro. All rights reserved.",
